      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>In simple words:</strong> House size and price form plotted points. Regression fits a line through the trend and estimates the price of a new house.",
      "technicalExplanation": "<strong>Detailed explanation:</strong> Given observed house sizes [50,75,100,125,150] square meters and prices [155,195,255,295,355] in thousands of dollars, ordinary least squares yields the line price=2×size+51. For 120 m², the predicted price is $291,000. This minimizes sum of squared vertical errors for the observed data. Real homes vary for many omitted reasons."
