      "tag": "Medium",
      "stem": "How can Linear Regression be implemented using Python and Scikit-learn, including preparing a dataset, dividing it into training and testing sets, fitting a regression model, generating predictions, visualizing the regression line, and evaluating results using MAE, RMSE, and R² Score?",
      "figure": "<section class=\"lr-figure\" data-scene=\"lr-05-sklearn-workflow\"><span class=\"lr-kicker\">VISUAL EXPLANATION</span><h3>Scikit-learn held-out evaluation</h3><div class=\"lr-svg-wrap\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 340\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scikit-learn held-out evaluation\"><rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"924\" height=\"324\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#fcfdfe\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"469\" y=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">TRAIN, TEST, AND MEASURE GENERALIZATION</text><rect x=\"21\" y=\"61\" width=\"212\" height=\"100\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"127\" y=\"97\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">DATA</text><text x=\"127\" y=\"129\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">14 rows</text><rect x=\"254\" y=\"61\" width=\"212\" height=\"100\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#fff2e7\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"97\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">SPLIT</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"129\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">10 train, 4 test</text><rect x=\"487\" y=\"61\" width=\"212\" height=\"100\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"593\" y=\"97\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">FIT</text><text x=\"593\" y=\"129\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">line</text><rect x=\"720\" y=\"61\" width=\"212\" height=\"100\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#fff2e7\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"826\" y=\"97\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">PREDICT</text><text x=\"826\" y=\"129\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">held-out</text><rect x=\"22\" y=\"185\" width=\"488\" height=\"133\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"264\" y=\"214\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">HELD-OUT TEST SCORES</text><rect x=\"41\" y=\"230\" width=\"135\" height=\"65\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#edf5fa\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"253\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">MAE</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"279\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">5.03</text><rect x=\"193\" y=\"230\" width=\"135\" height=\"65\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#edf5fa\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"253\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">RMSE</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"279\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">6.06</text><rect x=\"345\" y=\"230\" width=\"135\" height=\"65\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eaf8ee\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"412\" y=\"253\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">R²</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"279\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">0.996</text><rect x=\"530\" y=\"185\" width=\"389\" height=\"133\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d2e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"724\" y=\"212\" font-family=\"Arial,system-ui\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#426b80\">OBSERVED VS PREDICTED</text><line x1=\"559\" y1=\"294\" x2=\"884\" y2=\"294\" stroke=\"#94b4c0\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><line x1=\"559\" y1=\"294\" x2=\"559\" y2=\"228\" stroke=\"#94b4c0\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"578.5\" cy=\"284.1\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#74b4cd\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"640.25\" cy=\"272.88\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#74b4cd\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"711.75\" cy=\"262.32\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#74b4cd\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"786.5\" cy=\"245.16\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#74b4cd\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"858\" cy=\"232.62\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#74b4cd\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M578.5 284.1 L640.25 272.88 L711.75 262.32 L786.5 245.16 L858 232.62\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#68ac98\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg></div><p class=\"lr-note\">Use a test split and evaluate <strong>MAE, RMSE and R²</strong>.</p></section>",
      "options": [
        "Fit and test on identical rows, then report training accuracy as unbiased generalization performance.",
        "Split data before fitting, predict held-out targets, and evaluate errors, R², and the fitted line.",
        "Standardize the entire dataset before splitting, including the future test targets and their labels.",
        "Skip the test set and compare predictions with inputs, since the targets are unnecessary for regression."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>In simple words:</strong> Scikit-learn fits the line using training data, then predicts on held-out examples. MAE, RMSE, and R² check how well it performs.",
      "technicalExplanation": "<strong>Detailed explanation:</strong> Scikit-learn uses a NumPy dataset of fourteen homes and splits it into ten training and four test examples using random_state=42. The fitted LinearRegression was independently run: held-out MAE≈5.03, RMSE≈6.06 (both in thousands of dollars) and R²≈0.996. MAE is average absolute residual, RMSE emphasizes large errors, and R² measures explained variation relative to the mean baseline (and can be negative). Scores are high because this is a tiny toy dataset, not realistic production evaluation.<pre class='lr-code'><code>import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\nX=np.array([45,55,65,75,85,95,105,115,125,135,145,155,165,175],dtype=float).reshape(-1,1)\ny=np.array([138,168,174,210,226,251,269,273,310,323,334,364,379,395],dtype=float)\nX_tr,X_te,y_tr,y_te=train_test_split(X,y,test_size=.25,random_state=42)\nmodel=LinearRegression().fit(X_tr,y_tr)\np=model.predict(X_te)\nprint(mean_absolute_error(y_te,p)) # 5.03 ($thousands)\nprint(np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_te,p))) # 6.06\nprint(r2_score(y_te,p)) # 0.996\ngrid=np.linspace(40,180,200).reshape(-1,1)\nplt.scatter(X_tr[:,0],y_tr,label=&quot;Train&quot;)\nplt.scatter(X_te[:,0],y_te,label=&quot;Test&quot;)\nplt.plot(grid[:,0],model.predict(grid))\nplt.xlabel(&quot;Area (m²)&quot;);plt.ylabel(&quot;Price ($thousands)&quot;)\nplt.legend();plt.show()</code></pre>"
    },
